# Vite+

Vite+ 0.2.9 owns fmt, lint, typecheck, test, and the web dev server. Import
config from `vite-plus`. Do not add standalone Vite, ESLint, Prettier, or a
second Vitest.

```ts
// ✅ apps/web/vite.config.ts
import { defineConfig, lazyPlugins } from "vite-plus";

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: lazyPlugins(() => [react(), tailwindcss()]),
  server: {
    host: "0.0.0.0",
    port: 5173,
    proxy: {
      "/api": {
        target: process.env.API_PROXY_TARGET ?? "http://localhost:3000",
        timeout: 0,
        proxyTimeout: 0,
        configure: (proxy) => {
          proxy.on("proxyRes", (proxyRes) => {
            const contentType = String(proxyRes.headers["content-type"] ?? "");
            if (contentType.includes("text/event-stream")) {
              proxyRes.headers["cache-control"] = "no-cache, no-transform";
              proxyRes.headers["x-accel-buffering"] = "no";
            }
          });
        },
      },
    },
  },
});
```

- Root `vite.config.ts` owns workspace `fmt` / `lint` (Oxlint, including
  `vite-plus/prefer-vite-plus-imports`).
- Commands: `vp check`, `vp test`, `vp dev apps/web`, `vp build apps/web`.
